Package: csp-panel
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Recommends: nodejs (>= 18), nginx
Suggests: oscam
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: CSP Panel contributors <noreply@example.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/TalaveraSama/CSP-4.2
Description: Modern web panel for CardServProxy and OSCam
 A Java-free replacement for the legacy CardServProxy status web
 (cs-status.war), which also speaks the OSCam web API.
 .
 It ships a small Node service that talks to the softcam over its XML API
 (CSP /xmlHandler or OSCam /oscamapi.html, including HTTP digest auth),
 normalises both dialects into one JSON API, and serves a React single page
 application with overview, readers/connectors, sessions, channels, events,
 logs, admin commands and a configuration editor.
 .
 Credentials never reach the browser: they are kept in a server side session
 behind an opaque httpOnly cookie. The service listens on 127.0.0.1:8090 by
 default and is meant to be published through nginx.
 .
 Node.js >= 18 is required at runtime. It is only a recommendation because
 many setups install Node from nodesource, nvm or an upstream tarball rather
 than from the distribution package.
